            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#* So now we have a circuit with the resistors R<sub>s</sub>, R<sub>p1</sub>, R<sub>p2</sub> and R<sub>7</sub> connected in series. These can now simply be added to get the equivalent resistance R<sub>7</sub> of the network given to us originally.<br><br>R<sub>eq</sub> = 400 Ω + 20Ω + 8 Ω + 30 Ω = 428 Ω.<br><br>"
                ],
